      "internal": [
        {
          "severity": "nit",
          "file": "internal/gate/followup.go",
          "line": 98,
          "title": "Dead fallback in FollowUp.Key() for an error json.Marshal cannot produce",
          "detail": "Key() marshals a []any of only strings, ints and nil (see lines 90-97); json.Marshal cannot fail for those types (it only errors on channels, funcs, complex numbers, cyclic references or unsupported types), and the comment at lines 100-102 says as much (\"Unreachable\"). The fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", parts) fallback is therefore a legacy-style defensive branch that can never execute — a dead fallback per the over-engineering rubric (item 4). Not harmful, but it adds a branch and an unreachable format-based key-rendering path that will never be exercised by any test. Low priority: could simply be `b, _ := json.Marshal(parts); return string(b)` with a one-line comment noting why the error is ignored.",
          "lenses": [
            "simplicity"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
