          "detail": "The §3 table row `| error | — | unchanged: ask gate_review. |` and the §4 edge-case row at line 141 (`revise on the plan gate, or on a blocking/reject/error spec receipt | No event written; today's re-arm behaviour, unchanged.`) both describe the error verdict as still offering `revise` with the old re-arm behaviour. The diff's questionGateReviewErrored (internal/decide/questions.go) removes `revise` entirely for an error verdict and replaces it with a new `retry` choice that writes nothing and just tells the session to re-run the reviewer. Task 8's only edit to this file adds one sentence after this table (about carried findings), so the table itself and the edge-case row were left describing behaviour the diff just removed. A reader of this design doc would still expect `revise` to be offered on an errored spec review.",
